["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A bear's year is a race to get fat before the den. Know where it is in that race and you know where to look.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Black bear year by month. Denned roughly December to March. Leave the den April to May. Green up feeding April to June. Mating early June to mid July. Berries July to September and fall feeding, called hyperphagia, August to October. Den entry mid October to late November. Bars are approximate, from the BC account, WildSafeBC and a study just south of BC.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">The black bear year</text><text x=\"116.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"140.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text><text x=\"164.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"212.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"236.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"260.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"284.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"308.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text><text x=\"332.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text><text x=\"356.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text><text x=\"380.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Denned</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"73\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"104.0\" y=\"73\" width=\"79.19999999999999\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><rect x=\"356.0\" y=\"73\" width=\"36.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Den out</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"101\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"101\" width=\"40.8\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Green up</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"129\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"183.2\" y=\"129\" width=\"64.80000000000001\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mating</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"157\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"224.0\" y=\"157\" width=\"36.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Berries</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"185\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"255.2\" y=\"185\" width=\"84.00000000000003\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"227\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fall feed</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"213\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"272.0\" y=\"213\" width=\"72.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Den in</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"241\" width=\"288.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"332.0\" y=\"241\" width=\"36.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cubs are born in the den in January or February</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Den out in spring, green up, mating, berries, fall feed, den in <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Two seasons: spring and fall <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>January to December: the den, den out, spring green up, mating, berries and the fall feeding frenzy (hyperphagia), den in, and what October and November change.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-04\">Chapter 4, The mind</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-06\">Chapter 6, The day</a>.</li><li>Season dates come only from the Rule Book: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel of a black bear in four parts. Den: December to March, cubs born in January or February. Green up: April to June, the spring season. Berries: July to September, with mating in June and July. Fatten and den: September to November, the fall season. Seasons per the Rule Book for Region 3: spring 1 April to 30 June, fall 1 September to 30 November in most MUs.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 seasons of a bear</text><path d=\"M200 164 L108.1 72.1 A130 130 0 0 1 291.9 72.1 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"80.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Den</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"98.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec to Mar</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"114.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cubs born</text><path d=\"M200 164 L291.9 72.1 A130 130 0 0 1 291.9 255.9 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Green up</text><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr to Jun</text><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring hunt</text><path d=\"M200 164 L291.9 255.9 A130 130 0 0 1 108.1 255.9 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Berries</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul to Sep</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mating Jun, Jul</text><path d=\"M200 164 L108.1 255.9 A130 130 0 0 1 108.1 72.1 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fatten, den</text><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep to Nov</text><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fall hunt</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"164\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Den, green up, berries, fatten and den <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Spring hunt and fall hunt sit on each side of the den <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: seasons by region (no new rules)</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Spring</th><th>Fall</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3 (most MUs, Management Units)</td><td>Apr 1 to June 30</td><td>Sept 1 to Nov 30</td></tr><tr><td>3, MU 3-46</td><td>Apr 1 to June 30</td><td>Sept 20 to Nov 30</td></tr><tr><td>2, MUs 2-2 to 2-19</td><td>Apr 1 to June 15</td><td>Sept 10 to Nov 30; bow only Sept 1 to 9</td></tr><tr><td>8, MUs 8-1 to 8-15, 8-21 to 8-26</td><td>Apr 1 to June 30</td><td>Sept 1 to Nov 30; Aug 1 to 31 private land only</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>All rows 99% (pages 28, 34 and 68, 2 October 2026 edition), from the Rule Book: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8</a>.</li><li>Bag limit 2 per licence year, 1 April to 31 March, spring and fall together <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline of a black bear cub from the BC account. Mating early June to mid July. Delayed implantation: the embryo implants in October or November. Cubs born in the den in January or February, hairless and about 400 grams. Leave the den in spring at 2 to 5 kilograms. Weaned July to September. Den with the mother the first winter. On their own by the middle or end of their second spring.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">From mating to a bear on its own</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"66\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"91\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jun to Jul</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mating</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"99\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"107\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Oct to Nov</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Embryo implants</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"132\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"157\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jan to Feb</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Born, about 400 g</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"165\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Apr to May</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Out, 2 to 5 kg</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"198\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"223\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jul to Sep</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weaned</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"231\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"239\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"256\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2nd winter</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dens with mother</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"264\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2nd spring</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">On its own</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Cubs born in January or February, about 400 g <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Interior bears den about 5 to 7 months <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the den months in detail</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: hibernation \"three to five months on the south coast\" and \"probably five to seven months in the interior and the north\"; pregnant females den longest.</li><li>Cubs are born \"hairless, blind\" at about 400 g and nurse while the mother hibernates <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. WildSafeBC: 250 to 500 g, born late January <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Embryos implant only in October or November (delayed implantation), and only if the sow has enough fat (75 to 90%). A poor berry year can mean no cubs next winter (Tip, my reading).</li><li>Chapter 2 has the den body: heart, metabolism, weight loss.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Den dates in a study in the northeast Washington Cascades, next to the Okanagan (Gaines 2003). Into the den: females 15 October to 19 November, males 22 October to 19 November. Out of the den: females 4 April to 22 May, males 4 April to 7 May. Females, especially pregnant ones, den longer; males come out first.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Who dens first, who comes out last</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Into the den (fall)</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 15</text><line x1=\"211.6304347826087\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"211.6304347826087\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"211.6304347826087\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov 1</text><line x1=\"301.304347826087\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"301.304347826087\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"301.304347826087\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Nov 15</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Females</text><rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"76\" width=\"209.23913043478262\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Males</text><rect x=\"151.84782608695653\" y=\"106\" width=\"167.3913043478261\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Out of the den (spring)</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"192\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr 4</text><line x1=\"261.53061224489795\" y1=\"192\" x2=\"261.53061224489795\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"261.53061224489795\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May 1</text><line x1=\"379.38775510204084\" y1=\"192\" x2=\"379.38775510204084\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#c9c2b0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"379.38775510204084\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">May 22</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Females</text><rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"196\" width=\"269.38775510204084\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Males</text><rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"226\" width=\"185.20408163265307\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Males out first; sows with cubs last <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Lean and hungry: first green grass and forbs <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bb-cinnamon.jpg\" alt=\"Spring bear eating dandelions.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Spring bear eating dandelions. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Traveler100, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blackbearwaterton.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-skunk-cabbage.jpg\" alt=\"Skunk cabbage: early spring food on the coast.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Skunk cabbage: early spring food on the coast. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: The Cosmonaut, CC BY-SA 2.5 CA, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lysichiton_americanus_-_Aldergrove_Regional_Park.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: spring in detail</summary><ul><li>Den exit in the northeast Washington Cascades, next to the Okanagan: males 4 April to 7 May, females 4 April to 22 May (80%, Gaines 2003).</li><li>Alaska: females with cubs usually come out later than lone bears <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Spring food (90%, BC account): \"succulent vegetation in meadows, estuaries, riparian habitats, skunk cabbage swamps, avalanche chutes, grassy south facing slopes, and burned areas\".</li><li>WildSafeBC: grasses, sedges, horsetails; skunk cabbage <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Metabolism stays low for 2 to 3 weeks after den exit (80%, Alaska study): early spring bears move little (Tip).</li><li>Spring season opens 1 April in Regions 2, 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Early April bears are often still denned; late April and May are better (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Circles drawn to scale: an adult male black bear home range is typically 25 to 150 square kilometres, a female 5 to 25 square kilometres, from the BC government account. Big males roam widely; a sow stays in a smaller area.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Home range: boar vs sow (to scale)</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".18\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" r=\"41\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"200\" r=\"41\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".45\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"200\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Boar 25 to 150 km2</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sow 5 to 25 km2</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big males roam; a sow stays put (90%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mating early June to mid July <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Bears hunt newborn deer, elk and moose calves <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: early summer in detail</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: \"usually mate from early June to mid July\"; in spring they \"prey on newborn deer, elk, moose, and caribou\".</li><li>Mule deer study in the southern Interior: most newborn fawn deaths were from bears (85%, SIMDeer, via <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-01\">mule deer chapter 1</a>).</li><li>Boars travel widely and may be seen in daylight looking for sows (Tip).</li><li>Spring season ends 30 June in Regions 3 and 8 and 15 June in Region 2 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Sows with new cubs keep away from boars in the mating season (65%, chapter 4).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Berry calendar, July to December. Saskatoon and soopolallie: July and August. Huckleberry: August and September. Himalayan blackberry in the Fraser Valley: August and September. Rose hips and snowberry: fall into winter. Bears and grouse follow the fruit.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Berry calendar</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"160\" y=\"52\">Jul</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"52\">Aug</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"52\">Sep</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"52\">Oct</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"52\">Nov</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"52\">Dec</text></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M140 58 V270 M180 58 V270 M220 58 V270 M260 58 V270 M300 58 V270 M340 58 V270 M380 58 V270\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"132\" y=\"85\">Saskatoon</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"125\">Soopolallie</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"165\">Huckleberry</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"205\">Blackberry</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"245\">Hips, snowberry</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"70\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#5b3a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"110\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"150\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2c3e6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"190\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3d2a4a\"/>\n  <rect x=\"240\" y=\"230\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"268\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Fraser Valley</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bears and grouse follow the fruit (70%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Berries ripen low first, then higher up <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>A fall bear may eat up to 20,000 calories a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 292\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of calories per kilogram of wild fruit: huckleberry about 366, blackberry about 430, chokecherry about 549. In fall a bear may eat up to 20,000 calories a day, which is about 55 kg of huckleberries.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"292\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why bears eat all day in fall</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Huckleberry</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"50\" width=\"97.6\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2c3e6b\"/><text x=\"243.6\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">366 kcal/kg</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Blackberry</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"94\" width=\"114.66666666666667\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#3d2a4a\"/><text x=\"260.6666666666667\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">430 kcal/kg</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chokecherry</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"138\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6b1f2a\"/><text x=\"292.4\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">549 kcal/kg</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"186\" width=\"372\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Up to 20,000 calories a day in fall</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">That is about 55 kg of huckleberries</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear and berry figures via news (65 to 70%); my maths</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: summer and berries in detail</summary><ul><li>In summer, bears eat \"insects and larvae, fruits, berries, salmon, and carrion\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Soopolallie (soapberry) ripens late July to mid August and is a main bear food (65%, Sierra Club BC). Huckleberry fattens bears in August and September <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Berry timing follows elevation: valley bottoms first, high slopes later (70%, <a href=\"#/s/berries-mast\">berries and mast</a>).</li><li>The fall feeding frenzy, <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Hyperphagia\">Hyperphagia</button>, builds through August <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Region 8 only: August bear season on private land with the owner's permission (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"October versus November for black bears. October: most bears are still out, feeding on the last berries, fruit, apples and fish for much of the day, and sows with cubs start to den. November: many bears are denned, sows first and big males last; bears stay out only where food lasts, like orchards or fish; snow tracks show who is still up. The Region 3 fall season runs to 30 November.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">October vs November</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">October</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">November</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Most bears still out</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Last berries, fruit,</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">apples, fish</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeding much of</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">the day</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sows with cubs</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">start to den</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Many bears denned</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sows den first</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big males last</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Out only where food</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">lasts (orchards, fish)</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Snow tracks show</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">who is still up</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fall season runs to 30 November (Region 3)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fall season opens 1 September in most of Region 3 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Last berries, fruit and spawning fish <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><figure class=\"video\"><video controls preload=\"none\" playsinline src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/81/American_black_bears_%28Ursus_americanus%29.webm/American_black_bears_%28Ursus_americanus%29.webm.480p.vp9.webm\"></video><figcaption>Black bears at a salmon run in fall. <span class=\"credit\">Video: Bryon Evans, CC BY 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_black_bears_(Ursus_americanus).webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a>. Needs internet.</span></figcaption></figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: fall in detail</summary><ul><li>\"Come autumn, they often forage on berries and on spawning fish\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Fall foods near Kamloops (Tip, quick lesson): saskatoon, chokecherry, hawthorn, rose hips, kinnikinnick, fallen apples, Oregon grape.</li><li>Mast years and berry failures move bears: a poor berry crop sends them to orchards and towns (Tip).</li><li>Chapter 7 has the foods by place and month.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Black bear den calendar. Most bears are denned December to April, WildSafeBC. In a study just south of BC, bears left dens from 4 April to 22 May and entered dens from 15 October to 19 November. Cubs are born in January or February.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bear den calendar</text>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"111\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"124\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"135\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text>\n<line x1=\"146\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"157\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<line x1=\"170\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<line x1=\"194\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<line x1=\"218\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"218\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"229\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"241\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"241\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"252\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"266\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"266\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"276\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<line x1=\"290\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"301\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n<line x1=\"313\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"313\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"324\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text>\n<line x1=\"337\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"337\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"348\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text>\n<line x1=\"361\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"372\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Denned</text>\n<rect x=\"361\" y=\"59\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"59\" width=\"93\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Coming out</text>\n<rect x=\"173\" y=\"103\" width=\"37\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Going in</text>\n<rect x=\"324\" y=\"147\" width=\"27\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"207\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cubs born</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"191\" width=\"45\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Den out and in dates: northeast Cascades study (80%)</text>\n</svg></figure><ul><li>Sows in first; big males last <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Dens: tree cavities, rock, brush piles, dug holes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: denning in detail</summary><ul><li>Den entry near the Okanagan: females 15 October to 19 November, males 22 October to 19 November (80%, Gaines 2003). WildSafeBC: typically denned December to April, or November to April <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Some bears, often males, may not den if food lasts (75%, WildSafeBC).</li><li>Interior dens: tree cavities, or \"rock cavities, under brush piles, or in holes dug into the ground\"; coast dens are almost all in or under big old trees, logs or stumps, up to 25 m off the ground (90%, BC account).</li><li>\"When cold weather arrives, bears become increasingly lethargic and enter their dens\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Alaska: females with cubs den earlier and come out later than lone bears <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Bears doing</th><th>You do (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Early Oct</td><td>Feeding hard, much of the day</td><td>Glass berries and fruit, all day</td></tr><tr><td>Late Oct</td><td>Sows denning; boars still out</td><td>Focus on the best food left</td></tr><tr><td>Early Nov</td><td>Many denned; cold snaps</td><td>Fruit, fish, snow tracks</td></tr><tr><td>Late Nov</td><td>Mostly big males, few bears</td><td>Low odds; check tracks</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>The fall season runs to 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Big boars den last: late fall can be the best boar time (Tip).</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel of a black bear in four parts. Den: December to March, cubs born in January or February. Green up: April to June, the spring season. Berries: July to September, with mating in June and July. Fatten and den: September to November, the fall season. Seasons per the Rule Book for Region 3: spring 1 April to 30 June, fall 1 September to 30 November in most MUs.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 seasons of a bear</text><path d=\"M200 164 L108.1 72.1 A130 130 0 0 1 291.9 72.1 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"80.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Den</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"98.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec to Mar</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"114.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cubs born</text><path d=\"M200 164 L291.9 72.1 A130 130 0 0 1 291.9 255.9 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Green up</text><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr to Jun</text><text x=\"278.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring hunt</text><path d=\"M200 164 L291.9 255.9 A130 130 0 0 1 108.1 255.9 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Berries</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul to Sep</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mating Jun, Jul</text><path d=\"M200 164 L108.1 255.9 A130 130 0 0 1 108.1 72.1 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fatten, den</text><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep to Nov</text><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fall hunt</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"164\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Green in spring, love in June, berries by August, den by the cold moon.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 4 1 to 6 30, 9 1 to 11 30: Region 3 spring and fall <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, common hunting advice): \"Find the food, find the bear.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 400 g at birth, 2 to 5 kg out of the den (75 to 90%).</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 5 to 7 months in the den in the Interior <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Sows in first and out last; boars out first and in last.\"</li><li><strong>Tip</strong> (my reading of the den order data): a late November bear track in snow is most likely a male.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Hunting early April like it is May.</li><li>Glassing old food after the berries are gone.</li><li>Forgetting Region 2 spring closes 15 June.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>This October: visit one berry patch every week and note when the fruit ends and the bear sign stops.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2001), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/blackbear.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Black Bears in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Gaines (2003), Canadian Field Naturalist 117(4), <a href=\"https://www.canadianfieldnaturalist.ca/index.php/cfn/article/download/833/833/3326\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">black bear denning in the northeastern Cascades</a>, via <code>research/2026-10-03-migration-and-areas.md</code> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Alaska Department of Fish and Game, <a href=\"https://www.adfg.alaska.gov/index.cfm?adfg=blackbear.main\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Sierra Club BC, <a href=\"https://sierraclub.bc.ca/ecomap/soopolallie/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Soopolallie</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, via the Rule Book: pages 28, 34, 68 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Hunt Mentor lessons: <a href=\"#/s/berries-mast\">berries and mast</a>, <a href=\"#/s/black-bear\">Black bear</a></li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]